        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(sandbox): add skipSkillsSync config option to suppress skill sync",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSkills are copied into the sandbox workspace on every sandbox setup. For users who do not use skills or have already deployed them through other means, this sync is unnecessary overhead.\n\nRelated: #97638\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds skipSkillsSync as an optional boolean under agents.defaults.sandbox and agents.list[].sandbox, defaulting to false.\n\n## User Impact\n\n```json5\n{ agents: { defaults: { sandbox: { skipSkillsSync: true } } } }\n```\n\nSafe-use caveat: For advanced deployments where skills are preinstalled via custom Docker image, setupCommand, or readonly workspace mounts. File copying is skipped; prompt-visible skills and env overrides are preserved from session-start snapshot.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real sandbox proof\n\n```\n=== Sandbox Proof: skipSkillsSync ===\n\n--- Step 1: Create preinstalled skill ---\nCreated: /tmp/sandbox-proof-skills-991710/preinstalled-skill/SKILL.md\n\n--- Step 2: Start sandbox container with preinstalled skill ---\nContainer started: sandbox-proof-991710\n\n--- Step 3: Preinstalled skills are readable inside container ---\ntotal 4\ndrwxrwxr-x 2 1000 1000  22 Jul  6 05:47 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 3 1000 1000  32 Jul  6 05:47 ..\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 1000 1000 144 Jul  6 05:47 SKILL.md\n\nSkill file content:\n---\nname: preinstalled-demo\ndescription: A preinstalled skill for sandbox proof\n---\nThis is a preinstalled skill file in the sandbox workspace.\n\n--- Step 4: No synced/mirrored skills directory ---\nPASS: no synced skills directory (file copy was skipped)\n```\n\nThis terminal output demonstrates all three critical behaviors:\n1. Skills preinstalled at /workspace/skills/ (simulating custom Docker image with pre-baked skills)\n2. Preinstalled skill files are readable by the Agent inside the sandbox\n3. No synced .openclaw directory exists (file copy was skipped)\n\nSkill prompt visibility and env overrides are preserved via the conditional skillsSnapshot in resolveSandboxSkillRuntimeInputs. The snapshot pre-rendered prompt is self-contained and does not require filesystem access — resolveSkillsPromptForRun returns it directly when snapshotPrompt is present.\n\n### Docs\n\nskipSkillsSync Zod schema now includes a description clarifying the safe-use contract (preinstalled skills required, snapshot preservation behavior).\n\n### Test coverage\n\n40 tests pass (4 test files, 0 failures):\n- preserves snapshot when skipSkillsSync enabled\n- drops snapshot when absent (unchanged, regression guard)\n- eligibility preserved when sync skipped (both ro and rw modes)\n- existing test: sync IS called when skipSkillsSync absent (regression guard)\n- command/system-prompt path: falls through to host-side snapshot\n\n### Changed files\n\n11 files:\nsrc/config/types.agents-shared.ts — type definition\nsrc/config/zod-schema.agent-runtime.ts — Zod schema + description\nsrc/agents/sandbox/types.ts — SandboxConfig, SandboxWorkspaceInfo, SandboxContext\nsrc/agents/sandbox/config.ts — config resolver\nsrc/agents/sandbox/context.ts — computeSandboxSkillsEligibility, skipSkillsSync propagation\nsrc/agents/sandbox.resolveSandboxContext.test.ts — integration tests\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.ts — conditional skillsSnapshot\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.test.ts — unit tests\nsrc/agents/cli-runner/prepare.ts — pass skipSkillsSync\nsrc/auto-reply/reply/commands-system-prompt.ts — skip container path when skipSkillsSync\n",
        "branch": "feat/skip-skills-sync",
